        </figure>

        <h2 id="e"><span class="num">2</span>How it is tested</h2>
        <p>The model is trained to 2020-06 and evaluated strictly out of sample through 2025. Every test is a comparison that could fail: phase against magnitude and the other read-outs of the same predicted surface, the network against a parameter-free re-measurement of the realized scalogram, the coherence gate against a random selection of the same size, and the characteristic against twelve scalar-return systems under one protocol.</p>
        <figure>
          <img src="/projects/finphasor/media/era-emergence.png" alt="Bar chart of yearly gated rank IC by year, grey bars for the 2001-2011 placebo era averaging minus 0.010 and dark bars for 2012-2025 averaging plus 0.051, with stars marking years significant at t above 2." loading="lazy" decoding="async" style="margin:0 auto" />
          <figcaption><b>Figure 3.</b> The yearly rank IC of the gated phase lead. The 2001–2011 decade lies inside the training window and is null; the reading emerges after 2012 and is strongest out of sample, which is hard to square with overfitting. Figure from the manuscript.</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <h2 id="r"><span class="num">3</span>What it shows</h2>
        <div class="take">
          <div><h4>What held up</h4><ul><li>Phase, not magnitude, orders future returns; every other read-out of the same predicted surface is flat.</li><li>A zero-parameter re-measurement of the realized scalogram recovers the same ranking, so the network estimates something observable.</li><li>The coherence gate beats a random selection of the same size, so it is a reliability filter rather than a sampling effect.</li><li>None of the twelve scalar-return systems recovers the ordering.</li></ul></div>
          <div><h4>Where it stops</h4><ul><li>It is not claimed as a priced factor; the long–short alpha does not clear the paper's own multiple-testing bar.</li><li>The signal is era-conditional: null in 2001–2011, emerging after 2012.</li><li>It lives in the coherent large-cap core and weakens in the broader cross-section.</li><li>The news stream earns no predictive credit in ablation.</li></ul></div>
        </div>

